        "name": "USN-9097-1",
        "description": "It was discovered that Apache Commons Configuration enabled the script, dns, and url interpolation lookups by default. If an application used the default interpolation settings with untrusted configuration values, an attacker could possibly use this issue to execute arbitrary code or cause the application to contact remote servers. This update removes these lookups from the default set.",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2022-33980"
        ]
